    "title": "Penn State using bye week to 'get better' and prepare for White Out game vs. Oregon - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Hayden Sherry Allie Berube ,\n12 hours ago\n(WHTM) — Penn State football may be on a bye week, but they certainly aren’t taking the week off as the Nittany Lions focus on the fine details of the issues that plagued them through the first three weeks of the season.\n“This is a week to get better,” said head coach James Franklin. “We’ve always, Tuesdays and Wednesdays, have been work days, that’s how it will be for us. That’s how it should be all season. Whether it is a bye week or not.”\nThe workdays center around being better on offense and faster on defense. Penn State outscored its first three opponents, 132-17.\n“Yeah, obviously, with three new receivers, getting those guys comfortable and they’re building chemistry with Drew [Allar], we thought it was important,” said Franklin. “I think we’ve done a pretty good job at that, just the confidence and the execution of the new stuff on defense so that we can play fast.”\nFor Penn State to go where the Nittany Lions want to go this season, the tweaks after three games aren’t drastic here in Week four.\n“If all those guys make the plays that they’re supposed to make, and then if each one of them makes one special play a game, where they bring something more to the table than the o-line or the scheme got them, we’re gonna be in good shape,” Franklin said.\nOf course, no game for Penn State football this weekend, but they have their sights set on Oregon in the White Out on September 27.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WETM - MyTwinTiers.com.",
